{"metadata":{"title":"EntityStore","modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}],"role":"article","roleHeading":"Article"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore"},{"type":"text","text":" works like a dictionary with insertion-order iteration. Entities must conform to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Identifiable & Equatable & Sendable"},{"type":"text","text":" with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UUID"},{"type":"text","text":" as the ID type."}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["var cards = EntityStore<Card>()","","cards[card.id] = card                      \/\/ Insert or update — recorded","cards.modify(card.id) { $0.title = \"New\" } \/\/ In-place — recorded only if value changes","cards[card.id] = nil                       \/\/ Delete — recorded","","let card = cards[cardID]                   \/\/ O(1) lookup","let all  = cards.values                    \/\/ Insertion-ordered array","","cards.sort { $0.sortIndex < $1.sortIndex } \/\/ Only marks moved entities","cards.removeAll { $0.isArchived }          \/\/ Rebuilds index in one pass"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every mutation is tracked in a "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ChangeSet"},{"type":"text","text":" that the middleware drains after each reducer call."}]},{"anchor":"Bulk-Deletion","text":"Bulk Deletion","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"cards[id] = nil"},{"type":"text","text":" shifts the storage array’s tail and reindexes the shifted entries — O(tail) per delete, so a loop of k subscript deletes costs O(n·k). To delete many entities at once, use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"remove(ids:)"},{"type":"text","text":" (when you have the IDs) or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"removeAll(where:)"},{"type":"text","text":" (when you have a predicate) instead: both remove everything in a single pass with one index rebuild, record the same deletions, and cancel pending upserts exactly like the subscript."}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["cards.remove(ids: selection)          \/\/ One pass, not a subscript loop","cards.removeAll { $0.isArchived }"]},{"anchor":"Merging-Re-hydration","text":"Merging (Re-hydration)","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Replacing an "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore"},{"type":"text","text":" after startup destroys any in-memory state that was loaded lazily after initial hydration. Use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"merge(from:shouldReplace:)"},{"type":"text","text":" instead — entities only in the other store are always added, and the closure decides whether an incoming value overwrites the current one:"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["\/\/ Absorb DB rows; take an incoming row only when the current one","\/\/ lacks lazily-computed data.","campaigns.merge(from: EntityStore(allFromDB)) { current, incoming in","    current.calculationState == nil && incoming.calculationState != nil","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"merge"},{"type":"text","text":" does not record changes — it has hydration semantics like "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"init(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"anchor":"reconcile-vs-merge","text":"reconcile vs merge","type":"heading","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The two answer different questions:"}]},{"rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"merge(from:shouldReplace:)"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reconcile(with:preserving:removingMissing:)"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Stance"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Keep everything, absorb what’s new"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Storage is authoritative "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"except","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" where you say otherwise"}]}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Removes rows"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Never"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"removingMissing"},{"type":"text","text":" and the ID isn’t preserved"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Conflicts"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Your closure decides, per pair","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Storage wins unless the ID is preserved"}],"type":"paragraph"}]]],"header":"row","type":"table"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"reconcile","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is what lets a remote edit or a remote deletion surface mid-session rather than waiting for the next launch. "},{"code":"preserving","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is the caller’s list of IDs that carry unflushed local intent; the store’s own un-drained "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"changes"},{"type":"text","text":" are folded in automatically, so a pending local deletion is never resurrected even when "},{"code":"preserving","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is empty."}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["cards.reconcile(with: EntityStore(rowsFromDisk), preserving: dirtyIDs, removingMissing: true)"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Like "},{"code":"merge","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", it records no changes — every value it writes or removes already reflects what is in storage, so recording them would echo each remote change straight back as a local write.","type":"text"}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Most apps never call this directly; "},{"code":"PersistenceCoordinator.rehydrate(into:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" does, and computes "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"preserving"},{"type":"text","text":" for you."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"restore(from:)","anchor":"restorefrom"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"restore(from:)"},{"type":"text","text":" replaces all entities with those from the source store while recording the diff as changes for persistence. Used by undo\/redo (see "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoRedo","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":")."}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Deletions","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" — IDs in self but absent from source","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Upserts","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" — IDs that are new or whose values differ"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Unchanged","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" — identical values produce no change records"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"Remote-deletions-are-not-undoable","text":"Remote deletions are not undoable"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"One class of ID is skipped: anything ","type":"text"},{"code":"reconcile","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" removed because storage no longer held it. Those IDs are kept in ","type":"text"},{"code":"remotelyRemovedIDs","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and ","type":"text"},{"code":"restore","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" will neither re-add them nor record a change for them."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Without that, undo resurrects rows other devices deleted. An undo snapshot taken before the deletion still contains the entity, so restoring it records an "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"upsert","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — which flushes as a "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"creation","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" and re-seeds every peer that had already agreed the row was gone. Undo is scoped to what the local user did; a deletion made on another device isn’t that."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An ID leaves the set as soon as it becomes local again — an explicit "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store[id] = entity"},{"text":", or storage handing the row back on a later merge — so a row that another device deletes and then restores is undoable once more. The set survives ","type":"text"},{"code":"resetChanges()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", because a flush ends a pending write’s life, not a deletion’s."}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["\/\/ \"3 items were deleted on another device.\"","cards.remotelyRemovedIDs.count"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Stores that never sync never populate it, and ","type":"text"},{"code":"restore","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" takes exactly the path it did before.","type":"text"}]}]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStoreGuide"},"kind":"article","sections":[],"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Reference","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/MacrosReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginKillswitchReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginParentalGateReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginPaywallReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginAnalyticsReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginFeatureFlagsReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeyValueStoreGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoRedo","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/GettingStarted","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Troubleshooting"],"title":"Reference","generated":true}],"abstract":[{"text":"An ordered, keyed collection with built-in change tracking.","type":"text"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux\/entitystoreguide"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"]]},"references":{"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginPaywallReference":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginPaywallReference","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginpaywallreference","kind":"article","type":"topic","role":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"API reference for the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxPaywall"},{"type":"text","text":" library — paywall presentation, entitlement observation, and purchase orchestration."}],"title":"SwiduxPaywall Reference"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginFeatureFlagsReference":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginFeatureFlagsReference","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"API reference for the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxFeatureFlags"},{"type":"text","text":" library — typed feature flags, A\/B variants, and remote-tunable scalar values backed by a Swidux-defined JSON wire format."}],"role":"article","kind":"article","title":"SwiduxFeatureFlags Reference","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginfeatureflagsreference"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/UndoPlugin":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Snapshot-based undo\/redo plugin."}],"fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"UndoPlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"UndoPlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"UndoPlugin","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/undoplugin"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/ChangeSet":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ChangeSet","abstract":[{"text":"Tracks which entity IDs have been created\/updated or deleted.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ChangeSet","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ChangeSet","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"ChangeSet","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/changeset"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide":{"title":"Persistence Middleware","kind":"article","abstract":[{"text":"Configure automatic persistence that drains entity changes and batches database writes.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/persistencemiddlewareguide","type":"topic","role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/UndoRedo":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoRedo","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/undoredo","kind":"article","type":"topic","role":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Add stack-based undo\/redo to your app with "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"title":"Undo \/ Redo"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/Troubleshooting":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Troubleshooting","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Symptoms you may hit while adopting Swidux, and what each one actually means."}],"role":"article","kind":"article","title":"Troubleshooting","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/troubleshooting"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/KeyValueStoreGuide":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeyValueStoreGuide","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/keyvaluestoreguide","kind":"article","type":"topic","role":"collectionGroup","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Persist scalar preferences like theme, sort order, or last-seen version — testably, with type-safe keys."}],"title":"KeyValueStore"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/MacrosReference":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/MacrosReference","abstract":[{"text":"Reference for ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Swidux"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Slice","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (the observation bridge between value-type state and SwiftUI), and for ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Persisted","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and its property markers (the SwiftData persistence bridge, shipped in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxPersistence"},{"text":").","type":"text"}],"role":"article","kind":"article","title":"Macros","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/macrosreference"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/EntityStore":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An ordered, keyed collection of identifiable entities that silently records"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"every mutation for downstream persistence."}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"EntityStore","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"EntityStore","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"EntityStore","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/entitystore"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux","abstract":[{"text":"Redux-style state management for SwiftUI, with macros for observability and ready-made plugins for persistence, undo, paywalls, version killswitches, and parental gates.","type":"te